1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:02,842
A schema change should not become an incident.

2
00:00:02,877 --> 00:00:06,646
EvidenceGraph, an autonomous assurance agent, asks before merge:

3
00:00:06,681 --> 00:00:09,063
what will this change actually break?

4
00:00:09,544 --> 00:00:12,493
In our frozen synthetic seven-consumer truth set,

5
00:00:12,528 --> 00:00:14,796
repository search finds only three.

6
00:00:14,831 --> 00:00:18,368
It misses the dashboard, machine-learning feature, model,

7
00:00:18,403 --> 00:00:21,576
and deployment: a 42.9 percent view,

8
00:00:21,611 --> 00:00:23,540
and a false-safe decision.

9
00:00:25,199 --> 00:00:29,522
EvidenceGraph reads DataHub through the official MCP server and

10
00:00:29,557 --> 00:00:30,701
Python SDK.

11
00:00:30,736 --> 00:00:34,235
Schemas, ownership, lineage, contracts, dashboards,

12
00:00:34,270 --> 00:00:38,238
and ML metadata form an executable graph controlling scope,

13
00:00:38,273 --> 00:00:39,984
plans, and authority.

14
00:00:41,132 --> 00:00:45,347
Against that frozen truth set, DataHub grounds all seven impacts:

15
00:00:45,382 --> 00:00:49,063
two dbt models, Airflow, a dashboard, an ML feature,

16
00:00:49,098 --> 00:00:50,725
model, and deployment.

17
00:00:50,760 --> 00:00:55,235
Every path carries its owner, priority, and exact source object.

18
00:00:58,721 --> 00:01:02,929
EvidenceGraph compiles nine pull-request-ready drafts for human

19
00:01:02,964 --> 00:01:06,702
review, never auto-merged: SQL, dbt model and tests,

20
00:01:06,737 --> 00:01:11,107
validation queries, an Airflow evidence gate, an ML contract,

21
00:01:11,142 --> 00:01:14,189
migration plan, and a real unified diff.

22
00:01:16,812 --> 00:01:19,783
Fourteen deterministic gates run in DuckDB,

23
00:01:19,818 --> 00:01:23,898
dbt Core, the official Airflow container, feature-parity checks,

24
00:01:23,933 --> 00:01:26,423
and Git patch application. All pass.

25
00:01:26,458 --> 00:01:30,874
Remove one lineage page, and EvidenceGraph revokes proposal authority

26
00:01:30,909 --> 00:01:32,877
and blocks every mutation.

27
00:01:34,864 --> 00:01:38,555
With explicit approval in a controlled local DataHub run,

28
00:01:38,590 --> 00:01:43,600
a tag, description, and evidence document write back and verify by readback.

29
00:01:43,635 --> 00:01:48,106
A fresh client retries them: three verified no-ops, zero duplicates.

30
00:01:48,141 --> 00:01:52,138
A labeled closure replay closes only on a newer complete graph

31
00:01:52,173 --> 00:01:54,663
with zero retired-field consumers.

32
00:01:56,586 --> 00:01:59,795
EvidenceGraph turns DataHub into an observe, plan,

33
00:01:59,830 --> 00:02:01,756
validate, refuse-or-act loop.

34
00:02:01,791 --> 00:02:05,145
In the public deterministic replay, audit each claim,

35
00:02:05,180 --> 00:02:09,430
source object, confidence, test receipt, and unresolved risk.
